; Civil-date arithmetic, in one stdlib-only library: [seekwright.time], wrapped
; as [Seekwright_time], the third floor under the two big libraries beside
; [seekwright.text] and [seekwright.wire].
;
; It exists because the same Hinnant day-count had six copies here — [lib/usage.ml],
; four provider adapters, and [lib/cli/cli_metrics.ml] with the arithmetic inlined
; — and they had already drifted apart in spelling and in one sign. A module
; inside [lib/] could not be the owner: [seekwright.providers] and [seekwright.cli]
; link [seekwright], never the reverse, so nothing in [lib/] is reachable from an
; adapter.
;
; Stdlib-only like the other two floors: no clock, no timezone, no dependency on
; either big library. That is what keeps the recorded direction — [mcp-caps →
; seekwright → seekwright.providers / seekwright.fetch] — with the same floor
; under all of it. No timezone library is the recorded decision
; (plans/seekwright-ocaml-port.md); this module is that decision, not a new one.

(library
 (name seekwright_time)
 (public_name seekwright.time))
